            "annotations": [],
            "text": "{\n  \"decision\": \"request_changes\",\n  \"thresholds_preserved\": true,\n  \"contradiction_requires_evidence\": true,\n  \"controls_consistent\": false,\n  \"reason\": \"The protocol preserves the stated quality thresholds and correctly distinguishes missingness from contradiction: a contradiction requires a claim and explicit conflicting report text or authorized evidence, not absence alone. The custody, blinding, failure-retention, and no-retrospective-regrading controls are also well specified. However, the prospective calibration gate requires expected unit judgments, unit critical flags, report critical flags, and an additional-issues policy to match, while the control matrix supplies only D/V/C predicates and a Critical column. The expected calibration labels and their derivation are therefore underspecified for an exact 6/6 gate.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"issue\": \"The six-control matrix does not specify expected unit judgments or report-level critical flags, and it does not state the additional-issues policy, although the validation gate requires exact agreement on all of these.\",\n      \"action\": \"Before implementation or judging, add a frozen expected-label specification for every calibration control: unit judgment, unit criticalness, report criticalness, and the additional-issues policy. Alternatively, define deterministic derivations for these labels and make them part of the frozen calibration specification.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
